course: dictionary
lesson: 13151
title: The front wings of insects
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many insects have four wings. The two wings at the front are called forewings. «The butterfly flapped its forewings and rose into the air.» Fore means front, so the forewings are the front pair.
explain: The two wings at the back are called hindwings. «The moth's hindwings stayed hidden under its forewings while it rested.» Hind means back, so a hindwing is a back wing, and a forewing is a front wing.
explain: Beetles are different. Their forewings are hard, like a shell, and they cover and protect the delicate back wings. «The beetle's hard forewings clicked shut over its back wings.» It is still called a forewing, even when it looks like armour.
fact: A forewing is one of the two front wings of an insect with four wings.
fact: «Forewing» is made from «fore», meaning front, and «wing».
fact: Butterflies, moths, bees and beetles all have forewings.
fact: In beetles, the forewings are hard cases that cover and protect the back wings.
fact: Butterfly patterns often show on the forewings, so you can use them to tell butterflies apart.
exercise: «The butterfly flapped its forewings and rose into the air.» Which wings are the forewings? | The two back wings | The feelers on its head | *The two front wings | The two legs
exercise: In a beetle, what do the hard forewings do? | They are soft and clear like glass | *They cover and protect the back wings | They hold food in the mouth | They are the beetle's six legs
exercise: In the word hindwing, what does «hind» mean? | Front | Hard | Bright | *Back
test: Which of these insects has forewings? | A worm | A spider | *A moth | A snail
test: Which word means the back pair of wings? | Forewing | *Hindwing | Forehead | Front wing
exam: «The beetle's forewings were hard and shiny.» What do the forewings do in a beetle? | They make the beetle heavier | They help the beetle breathe underwater | They hold the beetle's food | *They cover and protect the back wings
